    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0430" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/123a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-04T15:00:00-04:00">November 4, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2065. Amdel 72. Personal for Secretary Hull<anchor n="92" xml:id="d386-f1"/> from
                    the President. I am in full accord with your suggestion that Bob Murphy be
                    appointed United States member of the Advisory Council to the Allied Control
                    Commission for Italy and further that he be given the rank of Ambassador. I am
                    telegraphing General Eisenhower to that effect. The State Department I
                    understand has telegraphed Murphy directly. I also agree that he be granted
                    leave before taking up his new job. Roosevelt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d386-f1" n="92" xml:id="d386-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary Hull returned from the Moscow Conference by way of North Africa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
